  "why": "The run is Mushoku Tensei: Jobless Reincarnation Season 3, a 14 episode TV run of summer 2026 that started 2026-07-04 and ends 2026-09-27, so it is still releasing on 2026-09-12 and several sources list only the 11 episodes broadcast so far. anizip:18727 is the same run: it maps SAME_AS to mal:59193 and anilist:178789, carries the same count of 14, and its episode dates run from 2026-07-03T15:00Z (2026-07-04 in Japan) to 2026-09-27, matching the run's start and end. cr:G24H1N3MP-GS00374452 is the same run: anilist:178789 itself maps SAME_AS to it, and its 11 episodes carry the same titles on the same dates as anizip:18727 episodes 1 to 11, from Burn Bright, Mad Dog on 2026-07-04 to Turning Point 4 on 2026-09-06. jw:222366-490814 is the same run: it maps SAME_AS to anilist:178789, mal:59193, kitsu:49002, offline:mal-59193 and anizip:18727, and its episodes 1 to 9 carry the same exact titles as anizip:18727 episodes 1 to 9, from Burn Bright, Mad Dog to Lament. cr:G24H1N3MP holds the run: it is the Crunchyroll series container (scope CONTAINER, a bare series id) and kitsu:49002 maps PART_OF to it. nf:80987039 holds the run: it is the Netflix series container (scope CONTAINER, titled Mushoku Tensei: Jobless Reincarnation with a start of 2021-01-01, covering the whole show), and jw:222366-490814 maps PART_OF to it. The episode pairs anizip 1 to 11 with cr 1 to 11 rest on equal episode titles and release dates at most a day apart, and anizip 1 to 9 with jw 1 to 9 rest on the exact, non generic titles; jw episodes 10 and 11 are only Episode 10 and Episode 11, so they are left unpaired, and the kitsu episodes carry neither title nor date, so they are left unpaired too. nf:80987039-3 is left unsettled: it lists 12 episodes against the run's 14 with no dates at all, its only non generic titles are Netflix's own translation (Rage, Mad Dog where the run has Burn Bright, Mad Dog), and every SAME_AS claim it makes is also made by the nf:80987039 container row, so the Netflix handles identify the show and not a season."
